<title>USA: Fix-Corp sees $15 mln in 1997 revs.</title>
<headline>Fix-Corp sees $15 mln in 1997 revs.</headline>
<dateline>BEACHWOOD, Ohio 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fix-Corp International Inc said on Wednesday its new plastics recycling division should put the company on track to achieve its 1997 revenue goal of $15 million.</p>
<p>The company had acquired a 50,000 square foot facility for plastics recycling on December 17, 1996, from Hanson Plc's Quantum Chemical Corp for $3.4 million, Fix-Corp said.</p>
<p>Revenues for 1996 totaled about $1 million, Fix-Corp said.</p>
